"""Build the self-contained review artifact from the completed isolated run."""
import base64, html, json
from pathlib import Path
E=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
m=json.loads((E/'metrics.json').read_text())
rows=[]
for name,a in m['assets'].items():
 rows.append('<tr><td>'+name+'</td>'+''.join('<td>'+str(a[t]['triangles'])+'</td>' for t in ('source','previous','refined'))+'<td>'+str(len(a['refined']['materials']))+'</td></tr>')
def image(name):
 return '<figure><img loading="lazy" src="data:image/png;base64,'+base64.b64encode((E/name).read_bytes()).decode()+'"><figcaption>'+html.escape(name)+'</figcaption></figure>'
body='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Vela foliage refinement 075</title>
<style>body{background:#f7f4ec;color:#17302f;font:16px/1.5 system-ui;margin:32px auto;max-width:1500px;padding:24px}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}table{border-collapse:collapse}th,td{border:1px solid #999;padding:8px;text-align:left}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:12px}img{width:100%;height:auto}figure{margin:0}figcaption{font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}code{font-size:13px}a{color:#07645a}</style>
<h1>Vela · foliage refinement · review only</h1>
<p><strong>HOLD adoption.</strong> The six new studies materially soften the yellow/mottled leaf response and replace inflated bloom beads with shallow scalloped corollas. These improvements are visible close up. At equivalent play scale the difference is modest, and B/C flowers visibly intersect the canopy. Reject B/C bloom presentation as finished art. Keep the material/leaf improvement for Redline/Glyph review; do not enable these candidates.</p>
<p>Only tools/decokit/recovery075_foliage.py and this new evidence folder were authored. Scratch FBXs/blend are under out/scratch/vela/foliage-refine. Production kit, Unity, Latch inputs, shared plants.py, restyle, source art and accepted captures were untouched. No whole-kit generation, model calls, Air or player/bot build.</p>
<h2>Recipe and material response</h2>
<p>Old/testbed plants.card and Cards bent-normal construction retained. Previous: 48 sprays per cushion, near-black #222D17 core, original unmodified photo colour, normal jitter .10; five inflated petal domes plus centre. Refined: 80 sprays, same deterministic lobe/flower calls, original civic-green core (#6A9B5C or #46794C), 75% civic green + 25% original source colour mixed in linear light, alpha &gt; .5, roughness .85, specular IOR .1; normal jitter .025. A spray is uniformly fitted about its own attachment during recipe construction against the original ten-sided lobe envelope. No per-axis clamp and no post-import mesh fitting.</p>
<p>Flowers use a 40-station, five-lobed shallow dish, outer radius r*(.70+.09*cos(5a)), rim height .18r, centre .10r, centre radius .16r; original seeded centres/radii/colours retained. Source texture remains full resolution, with unchanged bytes. Material copies use DK_Leaf_Refine075_Civic and DK_Leaf_Refine075_CivicDark; the node mix is not faithfully carried by FBX. Latch needs explicit review-only materials implementing the recorded mix; resolving them to unchanged DK_Leaf_Shrub would reproduce the rejected colour.</p>
<h2>Exact counts</h2><table><tr><th>Asset</th><th>Coarse source</th><th>Previous candidate</th><th>Refined candidate</th><th>Refined slots</th></tr>'''+''.join(rows)+'''</table>
<p>Counts are generated full meshes. Cypress is unchanged and not regenerated: the actual Unity baseline and prior candidate are both 5,004 triangles (+0). The unrelated 1,488 source comparison is not used. This is candidate recipe design, no decimation, compression, adopted-asset replacement or LOD edit.</p>
<h2>Bounds and integration delta</h2>
<p>metrics.json records every source/previous/refined XYZ envelope, material-slot list, per-material triangles, seeded call, FBX hash and source hash. Six source-envelope containment checks and six exact non-plant polygon-position comparisons pass. The original envelope constraints stay fixed; occupied mesh extrema are smaller/different, not falsely described as identical bounds. Two placement-aware preflights pass Latch's final 1 mm source-world-envelope constraints using its final selected IDs and current kit poses; cypress stays unchanged. This is an axis/pose preflight, not a new Unity FBX import proof. No excluded tuft is reintroduced.</p>
<p>The final three IDs remain civic/run-west-cafe/1 (PlanterRun_4_B), civic/civic-office-north/tuft-0 (BedTuft_A), civic/cyp-office-e (unchanged). Integration must retain original trough/trunk and copy only plant submeshes. delta.json computes proposed geometry against Latch's actual removed 612 and 95 triangles. Renderer and slot figures are proposed, not new scene measurements. Bounds, imported normals/UVs, material resolution and all attributes need independent import validation; no imported mesh may be clamped to pass.</p>
<h2>Controlled close comparisons</h2><p>Source / previous rejected candidate / refined. Same camera and illumination within this study. These are isolated Cycles asset studies, not Unity grade or whole-scene comparisons.</p>'''
for name in ('BedTuft_A','PlanterRun_4_B'):
 body+='<h3>'+name+'</h3><div class="grid">'+''.join(image(name+'-'+t+'-close.png') for t in ('source','previous','refined'))+'</div>'
body+='<h2>All six variants · refined close views</h2><div class="grid">'+''.join(image(n+'-refined-close.png') for n in m['assets'])+'</div>'
body+='''<h2>Equivalent play scale, full framing</h2><p>1920×1080, 38° pitch; vertical world span 28 m (Unity orthographic size14), horizontal 49.7778 m, headings30/210. Click/open the full PNGs for pixel judgment; fitting three columns makes them smaller than play size. No zoom crop substitutes for full framing. Trough detail remains modest at ~150 px width; tuft detail occupies only a few tens of pixels.</p>'''
for name in ('BedTuft_A','PlanterRun_4_B'):
 for yaw in (30,210):
  body+='<h3>'+name+' · yaw '+str(yaw)+'</h3><div class="grid">'+''.join(image(f'{name}-{t}-play-y{yaw}.png') for t in ('source','previous','refined'))+'</div>'
body+='''<h2>Evidence, limitations and handoff</h2>
<p>Guarded Blender -b -t4 check_render.py completed with FOLIAGE REFINE PASS, 22 renders. Full-resolution images above were inspected with view_image. The first sparse-shell study was rejected; two early geometry/preflight failures were corrected before final success (ten-sided source Y extrema and FBX handedness in preflight). The final render log and metrics are authoritative; command exit alone is not a pass. git diff --check passed for the scoped generator.</p>
<p>Close: smoother civic greens, fewer hard yellow rims, finer floral silhouette. Open: overlapping leaves form visible scalloped layers, some blooms look like thin discs and B/C blooms intersect foliage; these are not final approved art. At play scale there is no demonstrated large benefit over coarse source. 80 vs48 cutout sprays per cushion may increase overdraw despite lower total triangles. GPU time, alpha/shadow cost, draw calls, motion shimmer and Unity/URP colour equivalence are unmeasured. No 60 fps claim.</p>
<p>Redline/Glyph via Aster: review this report, metrics.json and delta.json before any further integration. Latch receives six scratch FBXs, material recipe and only the existing final-three placement constraints. Done-check: approve appearance, create explicit scoped review materials, validate actual imported/placed envelopes at1mm without fitting, retain non-plant attributes and existing transforms/colliders/nav, then measure moving alpha/shadow behaviour on settled content. No production enablement is included here. Source dense topiary sight behaviour remains HOLD. Potted topiary, palms and embedded planting remain open.</p>
<p><a href="metrics.json">Exact metrics</a> · <a href="delta.json">Latch proposal</a> · <a href="README.md">Commands and findings</a></p></html>'''
(E/'report.html').write_text(body)
